Derived data — CC-BY 4.0
========================

connectome.bin, positions.bin, inject-*.bin
-------------------------------------------
Derived from the FlyWire FAFB v783 connectome of the adult Drosophila
melanogaster brain, redistributed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0.

connectome.bin contains, for 138,639 neurons, the 2,700,513 synaptic
connections whose synapse count is >= 5, with the sign of each connection taken
from the predicted neurotransmitter. Weights are clipped to int8 (8,364 edges
saturate). positions.bin holds each neuron's soma position projected to 2D, used
only for visualisation. inject-*.bin maps board squares onto the visual relay
neurons that receive them.

Please cite:
  Dorkenwald et al. — Whole-brain annotation and multi-connectome cell typing
  of Drosophila (the FlyWire connectome)

The leaky integrate-and-fire parameters in meta.json follow:
  Shiu et al., Nature (2024) — a leaky integrate-and-fire computational model
  based on the connectome of the entire adult Drosophila brain

The visual cell-type inventory used to select the relay layer follows:
  Lappalainen et al., Nature (2024) — connectome-constrained networks predict
  neural activity across the fly visual system

